                <td>Ships 16 Nov; payload binding not stated</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p>Federal Reserve Governor Christopher Waller said on 28 September that the question becomes "proving that an agent has the authority to pay on the buyer's behalf."<sup><a href="#s7">7</a></sup> His remarks were a speech, not guidance. No enterprise procurement requirement appeared in the reviewed sources.<sup><a href="#s3">3</a>, <a href="#s4">4</a>, <a href="#s5">5</a>, <a href="#s6">6</a></sup></p>
